    "text": "Retransmission After = RBwmnsmrirery Ume ot > TCP maintains one retransmission time-out timer for all sent, but not acknowledged segments. > When timer matures, the earliest outstanding segment is retransmitted even though lack of a received ACK can be due to a delayed segment, a delayed ACK, or a lost acknowledgment. > No time-out timer ts set for a segment that carries only an ack. > The value of RTO 1s updated based on the round-trip trme of segments. Retransmission After Three Duplicate ACK Segments( fast retransmission) > If RTO ts very large, one segment is lost and receiver receives so many out-of-order segments that they cannot be saved (limited buffer size). > To prevent this, most implementations follow the 3-duplicate-ACKs rule and retransmit the missing segment immediately.",
